class Solution {
  public:
    int findEquilibrium(vector<int> &arr) {
        // code here
     int n=arr.size();
     int leftsum=0;
     int totalsum=0;
     for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
         totalsum+=arr[i];
     }
     int rightsum=0;
     for(int i=0;i<arr.size();i++){
        
         rightsum=totalsum-arr[i]-leftsum;
         if(leftsum==rightsum){
             return i;
         }
          leftsum+=arr[i];
         
     }
     return -1;
    }
};
Interview Explanation

"First, I calculate the total sum of all elements in the array. Then I traverse the array once. I maintain a variable leftSum which stores the sum of elements before the current index. To find the rightSum, I subtract the current element and leftSum from the total sum.

Formula:

rightSum = totalSum - arr[i] - leftSum

If leftSum becomes equal to rightSum, then the current index is the equilibrium index, so I return it. Otherwise, I add the current element to leftSum and move to the next index. If no such index is found, I return -1."
